<title>UK: Dixons slips on Tesco TV plans.</title>
<headline>Dixons slips on Tesco TV plans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in high street electrical retailer Dixons slipped on Wednesday after a press report said supermarket group Tesco was planning to start selling television sets in its stores.</p>
<p>Dixons shares fell 5-1/2p to 488p by 0901 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;The shares have come off purely on the press report of more competition,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>The Independent newspaper said that Tesco would begin selling television sets over the next two months. Its rivals, Asda and Sainsbury are already involved in the brown goods market.</p>
<p>--Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
